# Design Guidelines

## Component Structure
- Keep React components focused on one responsibility; extract reusable pieces when complexity grows.
- Place route-specific UI in its feature folder under `app/components`.
- Share repeated cross-route behavior with hooks or utilities instead of duplicating logic.

## Data And Service Boundaries
- Keep network and domain access logic in `src/lib` modules.
- Keep UI components presentation-first and pass in data/actions via props.
- Encapsulate plugin/native bridge behavior in dedicated plugin files.

## State And Side Effects
- Prefer localized state unless data must be shared broadly.
- Keep polling, timers, and async orchestration isolated and clearly named.
- Guard async flows against race conditions using cancellation flags or refs where appropriate.

## UI System Consistency
- Reuse existing design tokens and established panel/button conventions before introducing new patterns.
- For ride-along monitoring UI, keep waveform behavior encapsulated in `SpeechWaveform.tsx`.
